   <narrative xml:lang="EN">United Nations Industrial Development Organization</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Fostering Industry 4.0 for green transition and circular economy in the Western Balkans</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In the context of the innovation Agenda for Europe and the smart specialization, in order to support the Western Balkans in benefiting from the rapid development of frontier technologies and to strengthen linkages between science and business in the region, UNIDO proposes to foster regional economic and industrial integration and inclusion of emerging innovation ecosystems of Western Balkans and Eastern Partnership into a wider EU economic and technological landscape.  The Phase I of establishing the Smart Manufacturing Innovation Centre in Novi Sad involved several key activities. Initially, Terms of Reference were developed to establish a framework for developing a specialized hub that integrates regional expertise, fosters private sector collaboration, and supports manufacturing training and innovation in line with the country#s smart specialization strategy. In addition, strategic guidance was provided on how to develop a network of Smart Manufacturing Innovation Hubs in Serbia, leveraging expertise from universities in Slovenia and Serbia. Furthermore, a comprehensive training toolkit and e-platform were created to support SMEs, and a study tour to Slovenia was organized to promote collaboration and knowledge transfer. The official inauguration event of SMIC took place in June 2024. Over the course of two</narrative>
  </description>
